<div class="predictive-search__tabpanel focus-inset" id="psearch-{{ type }}" role="tabpanel" tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="psearch-{{ type }}-tab"{% unless forloop.first %} hidden{% endunless %}>
  <ul class="predictive-search__list" role="list">
    {%- for item in items -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        D-8 · formatos B2B (5/20 kg) fuera de la búsqueda B2C. Shopify NO trae
        un filtro nativo de "oculto solo en búsqueda" — el metafield
        `seo.hidden` (definición custom, boolean) que el admin marca en esos
        productos no hace nada por sí solo: hay que leerlo aquí y saltar el
        item. Solo pega en el panel PREDICTIVO (Section Rendering API); la
        página /search completa queda fuera del alcance de este sprint.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if type == 'products' -%}
        {%- capture fru_is_wholesale -%}{%- render 'fru-wholesale-handles', handle: item.handle -%}{%- endcapture -%}
        {%- if item.metafields.seo.hidden or fru_is_wholesale contains '1' -%}
          {%- continue -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign show_quick_add = false
        if type == 'products' and settings.enable_quick_add
          assign show_quick_add = true
        endif
      -%}
      <li class="predictive-search__item{% if show_quick_add %} flex items-center{% endif %}" role="option">
        <a class="predictive-result flex items-start focus-inset js-search-link{% if show_quick_add %} grow{% endif %}" href="{{ item.url }}"{% if settings.preload_links %} data-instant{% endif %}>
          {%- if type == 'products' or type == 'collections' -%}
            {%- liquid
              if type == 'products'
                assign img = item.featured_media.preview_image
              else
                assign img = item.featured_image
              endif
            -%}
            {%- if img != blank -%}
              <div class="predictive-result__media media relative{% if settings.blend_product_images and type == 'products' %} image-blend{% elsif settings.blend_collection_images and type == 'collections' %} image-blend{% endif %}">
                {{ img | image_url: width: 112 | image_tag: loading: 'eager', class: 'predictive-result__media' }}
              </div>
            {%- else -%}
              <div class="predictive-result__media media relative">
                {{ 'image' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'media__placeholder' }}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- elsif group_articles_pages or type == 'articles' -%}
            {%- if item.image != blank -%}
              {{ item.image | image_url: width: 112 | image_tag: loading: 'eager', class: 'predictive-result__media' }}
            {%- else -%}
              <div class="predictive-result__media"></div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          <div class="predictive-result__info flex-auto">
            <h3 class="predictive-result__title h6">{{ item.title }}</h3>
            {%- if type == 'products' -%}
              {%- if settings.predictive_search_show_price -%}
                {% render 'price', product: item, show_sale_color: settings.sale_price_color_quick_search %}
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if settings.predictive_search_show_vendor -%}
                <div class="predictive-result__sub-title text-sm">{{ item.vendor }}</div>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- elsif type == 'collections' and item.metafields.theme.label != empty -%}
              <div class="predictive-result__sub-title text-sm">
                {{ item.metafields.theme.label }}
              </div>
            {%- elsif item.url contains "/blogs/" -%}
              <div class="predictive-result__sub-title text-sm">
                {{ item.author }} | {{ item.published_at | time_tag: format: 'date' }}
              </div>
            {%- elsif item.url contains "/pages/" and group_articles_pages -%}
              <div class="predictive-result__sub-title">
                {{ 'templates.search.page' | t }}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </a>

        {%- if show_quick_add -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            BELLA-7 · quick-add en resultados de búsqueda. Mismo patrón que
            snippets/product-card-mini.liquid (icon-only, btn--sm), NO el de
            product-card.liquid: ese vive dentro del <a> que envuelve toda la
            tarjeta, y aquí el <a> (.js-search-link) envuelve toda la fila —
            anidar un <form> adentro dispararía el submit Y la navegación al
            mismo tiempo. .js-search-link tiene que seguir siendo hijo DIRECTO
            del <li> (lo usa predictive-search.js:180,
            `[aria-selected="true"] > .js-search-link`, para el Enter del
            teclado), así que el quick-add va como HERMANO del <a>, no adentro.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="predictive-result__quick-add shrink-0 pr-4">
            {%- if item.has_only_default_variant -%}
              {%- assign qa_variant = item.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}
              <product-form>
                <div class="alert bg-error-bg text-error-text js-form-error text-start" role="alert" hidden></div>
                {%- form 'product', item, class: 'js-product-form', id: 'psearch-quick-add-' | append: item.id, novalidate: 'novalidate' -%}
                  <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ qa_variant.id }}">
                  <button class="btn btn--secondary btn--sm btn--icon tap-target" name="add" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="{{- 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t | escape -}}"
                          {%- if qa_variant.available == false %} disabled{%- endif %}>
                    {% render 'icon-add-to-cart' %}
                  </button>
                {%- endform -%}
              </product-form>
            {%- else -%}
              <button type="button"
                      class="btn btn--secondary btn--sm btn--icon tap-target js-quick-add no-js-hidden"
                      aria-haspopup="dialog"
                      data-product-url="{{ item.url }}"
                      data-product-id="{{ item.id }}"
                      aria-label="{{- 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t | escape -}}">
                {% render 'icon-add-to-cart' %}
              </button>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
    <li class="predictive-search__item js-submit" role="option">
      <button class="predictive-search__view-all link w-full text-start focus-inset has-ltr-icon js-search-link">
        {{- 'general.search.view_all' | t -}} {% render 'icon-arrow-right' %}
      </button>
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>
